From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:36:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Census the top-level winemetal API and zero sidecar padding

The API census counts every call across the single PE-to-unix boundary, so all
114 entries are measured consistently rather than by instrumenting call sites
one at a time, and classifies each as producer, consumer, lifetime, query,
sync, presentation or bulk memory. Names are generated from the same dispatch
table the codes index; a second hand-numbered list would drift and silently
attribute calls to the wrong function, which is worse than no census. It also
records the first calls in ORDER, since the control plane has to be
reimplemented in sequence and a frequency table does not show that.

Counters are atomic and reporting is summary-only: resource and pipeline work
may be multithreaded even where rendering is not, and per-call logging would
distort the workload being measured.

This exists because a packed command batch carries guest handles, which are raw
pointer casts and meaningless on another machine. Every handle producer and
consumer has to move together -- a half-switched state mixes address spaces and
fails as a wrong-looking frame rather than an error.

Also zeroes the sidecar alignment padding. The cursor was advanced to an 8-byte
boundary without clearing the skipped bytes, and because the buffer is reused
those bytes still held data from an earlier batch and were transmitted as part
of the sidecar region -- stale guest data on the wire, and a payload that
differed run to run for identical input.

